item.on_dock_branch:
The read is gone on bl/dock/wi8 @ 575084358. 817f555c3 deletes dockMorphMeasure.ts, and nothing in src/components/dock reads document.fonts. The only getter left in src is src/components/handmark/HandMark.vue:497.

Its successor still reads at mount. GlassDock.vue:196 calls `useDockBody({...})`, and useDockBody.ts:1326-1328 runs `onMounted(() => { ... sync("mount") })` inside the mount task. sync reads:
- rectOf(el) at :730 (getBoundingClientRect at :161);
- roomOf at :733 when the fit was just decided;
- `getComputedStyle(el).direction` at :749;
- restRadius's borderTopLeftRadius at :262;
- readSeats at :763.

On a collapsed dock (the /speedtest case), fitRun returns at :524 before it reads anything, so that is one forced style and layout in the mount task. An open run reads fitRun first (offsetParent and the seat offsets, :524-535), and the read is taken twice when its fit flag changes.

This breaks O-122 G-17's booked law (W-0.8.md:252: no forced layout inside GlassDock's mount task). It is the object of the wi8 ledger's L-60 (O-180 (3), O-215: no forced layout at first mount above 16 ms). Its cost is not measured, since no wi8 trace exists.
